{"t":"2026-05-28T03:45:49.583Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016vVLkYj3SYVSAeypkc4yYw","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-CRAWLER\n     2→\n     3→> HYPHA tag: `TA/SYNTH-CRAWL`\n     4→> Maps to Mycelium agent: `synthetics-crawler-agent`\n     5→\n     6→## Goal\n     7→\n     8→Own the upstream health monitoring harness. Exercise the live crawler endpoints (Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby) hourly with lightweight HEAD-equivalent requests, track consecutive failures via a state machine, and alert on 3-strike threshold. This biome is the sentinel: if an upstream API changes, rate-limits, or breaks — the crawler harness detects it within 3 hours.\n     9→\n    10→## Scope\n    11→\n    12→### In Scope\n    13→\n    14→- `backend/synthetics/crawler_health.py` — `CrawlerHealthRunner.run_suite()` health check orchestration\n    15→- `backend/synthetics/expected_schema_v1.json` — expected response shapes for Greenhouse/Lever/Ashby\n    16→- `synthetics/state.json` — persistent state file tracking consecutive failures per source\n    17→- `backend/synthetics/beat_schedule.py` — Celery beat extension for hourly crawler health + daily scoring\n    18→- `backend/synthetics/cli.py` extension — `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=crawler`\n    19→\n    20→### Out of Scope\n    21→\n    22→- Synthetic candidate fixtures (owned by `synthetics-fixtures-agent`)\n    23→- Scoring drift detection (owned by `synthetics-scoring-agent`)\n    24→- Workday health checks — Playwright is too expensive for hourly. Workday exercises daily via scoring suite.\n    25→- Modifying the frozen `scheduler-agent` beat schedule — use additive registration only\n    26→- Schema changes — no new tables, no new columns\n    27→\n    28→## Inputs\n    29→\n    30→- `discover-agent` (FROZEN): Crawler adapter implementations for API endpoint patterns\n    31→- `obs-agent` (FROZEN): `publish_event(channel, payload)` for health alerts\n    32→- `NUTRIENTS.md §I.6`: Crawler health contract, state machine rules\n    33→\n    34→## Outputs (Deliverables)\n    35→\n    36→- `backend/synthetics/crawler_health.py`\n    37→- `backend/synthetics/expected_schema_v1.json`\n    38→- `backend/synthetics/beat_schedule.py`\n    39→- `synthetics/state.json`\n    40→- `synthetics/runs/<ts>/crawler-report.json` — per-run health reports\n    41→\n    42→## Acceptance Criteria\n    43→\n    44→- [ ] `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=crawler` produces `synthetics/runs/<ts>/crawler-report.json`\n    45→- [ ] Report contains per-source `{status, latency_ms, schema_match, sample_jobs, error}`\n    46→- [ ] `curl http://localhost:8000/events/stream?channel=agent.status.synthetics.crawler` shows health pings during manual run\n    47→- [ ] Pointing the suite at a deliberately-wrong slug produces `status: failed, consecutive_failures: 1` — no alert\n    48→- [ ] Three consecutive failures for the same source produces `status: red, consecutive_failures: 3` — publishes alert\n    49→- [ ] A success after 3 failures resets to `status: green, consecutive_failures: 0` — publishes recovery event\n    50→- [ ] `cat synthetics/state.json` shows `consecutive_failures: 0` for all sources after successful run\n    51→- [ ] Hourly Celery beat entry is registered additively (does not modify frozen `daily_discovery_task`)\n    52→- [ ] No `print()` anywhere — `structlog` only\n    53→- [ ] `ruff check backend/synthetics/` clean\n    54→- [ ] `pytest tests/synthetics/ -v` → exit 0\n    55→\n    56→## Notes\n    57→\n    58→### Health Check Targets\n    59→\n    60→| Source | Slug | Endpoint | Method | Expected shape |\n    61→|---|---|---|---|---|\n    62→| Greenhouse | `anthropic` | `https://boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic.json` | GET | `{jobs: [...]}` |\n    63→| Lever | `netflix` | `https://api.lever.co/v0/postings/netflix?limit=1` | GET | `[{id, text, ...}]` |\n    64→| Ashby | `posthog` | `https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/posthog` | GET | `{jobs: [...]}` |\n    65→\n    66→Note: Lever uses `?limit=1` to minimize data transfer while validating schema.\n    67→\n    68→### State Machine\n    69→\n    70→```python\n    71→@dataclass\n    72→class CrawlerHealthState:\n    73→    source: str  # 'greenhouse' | 'lever' | 'ashby'\n    74→    status: str  # 'green' | 'red'\n    75→    consecutive_failures: int\n    76→    last_success: str | None  # ISO-8601\n    77→    last_failure: str | None  # ISO-8601\n    78→    last_error: str | None\n    79→```\n    80→\n    81→**Transition rules:**\n    82→```\n    83→on_success:\n    84→    consecutive_failures = 0\n    85→    status = 'green'\n    86→    last_success = now()\n    87→    if previous.status == 'red':\n    88→        publish_recovery_event()\n    89→\n    90→on_failure:\n    91→    consecutive_failures += 1\n    92→    last_failure = now()\n    93→    last_error = error_message\n    94→    if consecutive_failures >= 3 and previous.status != 'red':\n    95→        status = 'red'\n    96→        publish_alert_event()\n    97→```\n    98→\n    99→### State Persistence\n   100→\n   101→`synthetics/state.json` is persistent across runs:\n   102→\n   103→```json\n   104→{\n   105→  \"greenhouse\": {\n   106→    \"status\": \"green\",\n   107→    \"consecutive_failures\": 0,\n   108→    \"last_success\": \"2026-05-28T03:00:00Z\",\n   109→    \"last_failure\": null,\n   110→    \"last_error\": null\n   111→  },\n   112→  \"lever\": {\n   113→    \"status\": \"green\",\n   114→    \"consecutive_failures\": 0,\n   115→    \"last_success\": \"2026-05-28T03:00:00Z\",\n   116→    \"last_failure\": null,\n   117→    \"last_error\": null\n   118→  },\n   119→  \"ashby\": {\n   120→    \"status\": \"green\",\n   121→    \"consecutive_failures\": 0,\n   122→    \"last_success\": \"2026-05-28T03:00:00Z\",\n   123→    \"last_failure\": null,\n   124→    \"last_error\": null\n   125→  }\n   126→}\n   127→```\n   128→\n   129→If the file doesn't exist, initialize with all sources green + zero failures.\n   130→\n   131→### Schema Validation\n   132→\n   133→`expected_schema_v1.json`:\n   134→\n   135→```json\n   136→{\n   137→  \"greenhouse\": {\n   138→    \"type\": \"object\",\n   139→    \"required\": [\"jobs\"],\n   140→    \"properties\": {\n   141→      \"jobs\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1}\n   142→    }\n   143→  },\n   144→  \"lever\": {\n   145→    \"type\": \"array\",\n   146→    \"minItems\": 1,\n   147→    \"items\": {\n   148→      \"type\": \"object\",\n   149→      \"required\": [\"id\"]\n   150→    }\n   151→  },\n   152→  \"ashby\": {\n   153→    \"type\": \"object\",\n   154→    \"required\": [\"jobs\"],\n   155→    \"properties\": {\n   156→      \"jobs\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1}\n   157→    }\n   158→  }\n   159→}\n   160→```\n   161→\n   162→Use `jsonschema` for validation. Schema match = True only if response validates against expected shape AND `jobs` array (or root array for Lever) has ≥1 entry.\n   163→\n   164→### Beat Schedule Extension\n   165→\n   166→`backend/synthetics/beat_schedule.py`:\n   167→\n   168→```python\n   169→from celery import Celery\n   170→from celery.schedules import crontab\n   171→\n   172→def register_synthetics_beat(app: Celery) -> None:\n   173→    \"\"\"Additively register synthetics tasks on the Celery beat schedule.\n   174→\n   175→    Does NOT modify frozen scheduler-agent entries.\n   176→    \"\"\"\n   177→    app.conf.beat_schedule.update({\n   178→        'synthetics-crawler-hourly': {\n   179→            'task': 'backend.synthetics.tasks.crawler_health_task',\n   180→            'schedule': crontab(minute=0),  # Every hour on the hour\n   181→            'options': {'queue': 'default'}\n   182→        },\n   183→        'synthetics-scoring-daily': {\n   184→            'task': 'backend.synthetics.tasks.scoring_suite_task',\n   185→            'schedule': crontab(hour=3, minute=0),  # 03:00 UTC\n   186→            'options': {'queue': 'default'}\n   187→        }\n   188→    })\n   189→```\n   190→\n   191→This function is called from `backend/main.py` lifespan after the Celery app is imported:\n   192→\n   193→```python\n   194→from backend.synthetics.beat_schedule import register_synthetics_beat\n   195→from backend.scheduler.celery_app import celery_app\n   196→\n   197→register_synthetics_beat(celery_app)\n   198→```\n   199→\n   200→### Alert Events\n   201→\n   202→Published to Redis pub/sub channel `agent.status.synthetics.crawler`:\n   203→\n   204→```python\n   205→# Alert (red)\n   206→{\n   207→    \"source\": \"greenhouse\",\n   208→    \"status\": \"red\",\n   209→    \"consecutive_failures\": 3,\n   210→    \"error\": \"HTTP 429 Too Many Requests\",\n   211→    \"ts\": \"2026-05-28T04:00:00Z\"\n   212→}\n   213→\n   214→# Recovery (green)\n   215→{\n   216→    \"source\": \"greenhouse\",\n   217→    \"status\": \"green\",\n   218→    \"consecutive_failures\": 0,\n   219→    \"ts\": \"2026-05-28T05:00:00Z\"\n   220→}\n   221→```\n   222→\n   223→### Why Not Workday?\n   224→\n   225→Workday requires Playwright for browser automation. Running Playwright hourly is:\n   226→1. Expensive (compute cost)\n   227→2. Slow (~30s per check vs ~200ms for API endpoints)\n   228→3. Flaky (browser automation is inherently less stable)\n   229→\n   230→Workday is exercised daily via the scoring suite. If Workday breaks, the scoring fingerprint will drift on the Workday-sourced JDs.\n   231→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3d85e71-547f-47fc-9b8e-03f9b792b0cb","uuid":"cfc56156-847c-4a7d-a9cc-da52ab7c2a8b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/hyphae/HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-CRAWLER.md","content":"# HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-CRAWLER\n\n> HYPHA tag: `TA/SYNTH-CRAWL`\n> Maps to Mycelium agent: `synthetics-crawler-agent`\n\n## Goal\n\nOwn the upstream health monitoring harness. Exercise the live crawler endpoints (Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby) hourly with lightweight HEAD-equivalent requests, track consecutive failures via a state machine, and alert on 3-strike threshold. This biome is the sentinel: if an upstream API changes, rate-limits, or breaks — the crawler harness detects it within 3 hours.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In Scope\n\n- `backend/synthetics/crawler_health.py` — `CrawlerHealthRunner.run_suite()` health check orchestration\n- `backend/synthetics/expected_schema_v1.json` — expected response shapes for Greenhouse/Lever/Ashby\n- `synthetics/state.json` — persistent state file tracking consecutive failures per source\n- `backend/synthetics/beat_schedule.py` — Celery beat extension for hourly crawler health + daily scoring\n- `backend/synthetics/cli.py` extension — `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=crawler`\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- Synthetic candidate fixtures (owned by `synthetics-fixtures-agent`)\n- Scoring drift detection (owned by `synthetics-scoring-agent`)\n- Workday health checks — Playwright is too expensive for hourly. Workday exercises daily via scoring suite.\n- Modifying the frozen `scheduler-agent` beat schedule — use additive registration only\n- Schema changes — no new tables, no new columns\n\n## Inputs\n\n- `discover-agent` (FROZEN): Crawler adapter implementations for API endpoint patterns\n- `obs-agent` (FROZEN): `publish_event(channel, payload)` for health alerts\n- `NUTRIENTS.md §I.6`: Crawler health contract, state machine rules\n\n## Outputs (Deliverables)\n\n- `backend/synthetics/crawler_health.py`\n- `backend/synthetics/expected_schema_v1.json`\n- `backend/synthetics/beat_schedule.py`\n- `synthetics/state.json`\n- `synthetics/runs/<ts>/crawler-report.json` — per-run health reports\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=crawler` produces `synthetics/runs/<ts>/crawler-report.json`\n- [ ] Report contains per-source `{status, latency_ms, schema_match, sample_jobs, error}`\n- [ ] `curl http://localhost:8000/events/stream?channel=agent.status.synthetics.crawler` shows health pings during manual run\n- [ ] Pointing the suite at a deliberately-wrong slug produces `status: failed, consecutive_failures: 1` — no alert\n- [ ] Three consecutive failures for the same source produces `status: red, consecutive_failures: 3` — publishes alert\n- [ ] A success after 3 failures resets to `status: green, consecutive_failures: 0` — publishes recovery event\n- [ ] `cat synthetics/state.json` shows `consecutive_failures: 0` for all sources after successful run\n- [ ] Hourly Celery beat entry is registered additively (does not modify frozen `daily_discovery_task`)\n- [ ] No `print()` anywhere — `structlog` only\n- [ ] `ruff check backend/synthetics/` clean\n- [ ] `pytest tests/synthetics/ -v` → exit 0\n\n## Notes\n\n### Health Check Targets\n\n| Source | Slug | Endpoint | Method | Expected shape |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Greenhouse | `anthropic` | `https://boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic.json` | GET | `{jobs: [...]}` |\n| Lever | `netflix` | `https://api.lever.co/v0/postings/netflix?limit=1` | GET | `[{id, text, ...}]` |\n| Ashby | `posthog` | `https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/posthog` | GET | `{jobs: [...]}` |\n\nNote: Lever uses `?limit=1` to minimize data transfer while validating schema.\n\n### State Machine\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass CrawlerHealthState:\n    source: str  # 'greenhouse' | 'lever' | 'ashby'\n    status: str  # 'green' | 'red'\n    consecutive_failures: int\n    last_success: str | None  # ISO-8601\n    last_failure: str | None  # ISO-8601\n    last_error: str | None\n```\n\n**Transition rules:**\n```\non_success:\n    consecutive_failures = 0\n    status = 'green'\n    last_success = now()\n    if previous.status == 'red':\n        publish_recovery_event()\n\non_failure:\n    consecutive_failures += 1\n    last_failure = now()\n    last_error = error_message\n    if consecutive_failures >= 3 and previous.status != 'red':\n        status = 'red'\n        publish_alert_event()\n```\n\n### State Persistence\n\n`synthetics/state.json` is persistent across runs:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"greenhouse\": {\n    \"status\": \"green\",\n    \"consecutive_failures\": 0,\n    \"last_success\": \"2026-05-28T03:00:00Z\",\n    \"last_failure\": null,\n    \"last_error\": null\n  },\n  \"lever\": {\n    \"status\": \"green\",\n    \"consecutive_failures\": 0,\n    \"last_success\": \"2026-05-28T03:00:00Z\",\n    \"last_failure\": null,\n    \"last_error\": null\n  },\n  \"ashby\": {\n    \"status\": \"green\",\n    \"consecutive_failures\": 0,\n    \"last_success\": \"2026-05-28T03:00:00Z\",\n    \"last_failure\": null,\n    \"last_error\": null\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIf the file doesn't exist, initialize with all sources green + zero failures.\n\n### Schema Validation\n\n`expected_schema_v1.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"greenhouse\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"required\": [\"jobs\"],\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"jobs\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1}\n    }\n  },\n  \"lever\": {\n    \"type\": \"array\",\n    \"minItems\": 1,\n    \"items\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"id\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"ashby\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"required\": [\"jobs\"],\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"jobs\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1}\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nUse `jsonschema` for validation. Schema match = True only if response validates against expected shape AND `jobs` array (or root array for Lever) has ≥1 entry.\n\n### Beat Schedule Extension\n\n`backend/synthetics/beat_schedule.py`:\n\n```python\nfrom celery import Celery\nfrom celery.schedules import crontab\n\ndef register_synthetics_beat(app: Celery) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Additively register synthetics tasks on the Celery beat schedule.\n\n    Does NOT modify frozen scheduler-agent entries.\n    \"\"\"\n    app.conf.beat_schedule.update({\n        'synthetics-crawler-hourly': {\n            'task': 'backend.synthetics.tasks.crawler_health_task',\n            'schedule': crontab(minute=0),  # Every hour on the hour\n            'options': {'queue': 'default'}\n        },\n        'synthetics-scoring-daily': {\n            'task': 'backend.synthetics.tasks.scoring_suite_task',\n            'schedule': crontab(hour=3, minute=0),  # 03:00 UTC\n            'options': {'queue': 'default'}\n        }\n    })\n```\n\nThis function is called from `backend/main.py` lifespan after the Celery app is imported:\n\n```python\nfrom backend.synthetics.beat_schedule import register_synthetics_beat\nfrom backend.scheduler.celery_app import celery_app\n\nregister_synthetics_beat(celery_app)\n```\n\n### Alert Events\n\nPublished to Redis pub/sub channel `agent.status.synthetics.crawler`:\n\n```python\n# Alert (red)\n{\n    \"source\": \"greenhouse\",\n    \"status\": \"red\",\n    \"consecutive_failures\": 3,\n    \"error\": \"HTTP 429 Too Many Requests\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-05-28T04:00:00Z\"\n}\n\n# Recovery (green)\n{\n    \"source\": \"greenhouse\",\n    \"status\": \"green\",\n    \"consecutive_failures\": 0,\n    \"ts\": \"2026-05-28T05:00:00Z\"\n}\n```\n\n### Why Not Workday?\n\nWorkday requires Playwright for browser automation. Running Playwright hourly is:\n1. Expensive (compute cost)\n2. Slow (~30s per check vs ~200ms for API endpoints)\n3. Flaky (browser automation is inherently less stable)\n\nWorkday is exercised daily via the scoring suite. If Workday breaks, the scoring fingerprint will drift on the Workday-sourced JDs.\n","numLines":231,"startLine":1,"totalLines":231}}}}
