{"t":"2026-05-28T03:46:01.278Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LNGUzNwCRsLTLFBWsaYJMR","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n     2→\n     3→\"\"\"\n     4→Web Crawler Agent — multi-source job board crawler.\n     5→\n     6→Supported sources:\n     7→  1. Greenhouse (boards.greenhouse.io/{slug}.json) — public JSON\n     8→  2. Lever (api.lever.co/v0/postings/{slug}?mode=json) — public JSON\n     9→  3. Ashby (api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/{slug}) — public JSON\n    10→  4. Workday — deferred (Playwright crawl; not in this revision)\n    11→\n    12→Rate limits: 2 req/sec per host, 0.5-2.0s jitter, User-Agent\n    13→\"TalentAgent/1.0 (+https://github.com/example/talent-agent)\". Adapters\n    14→fan out concurrently across slugs with a semaphore of 4 per source.\n    15→\n    16→Dedup: url_hash() against the discovered_jobs table before insert.\n    17→Curated company slugs live in backend/agents/discovery/sources.yaml.\n    18→\n    19→Offline fallback: if all live adapters return zero rows (network down,\n    20→all sources rate-limited), CrawlerAgent falls back to the FIXTURE_JOBS\n    21→roster so dev pipelines still produce data. Production should monitor\n    22→for this fallback via the `crawler.fallback_used` structured log event.\n    23→\"\"\"\n    24→\n    25→import asyncio\n    26→import hashlib\n    27→import html\n    28→import random\n    29→from datetime import datetime, timezone\n    30→from pathlib import Path\n    31→from typing import Optional\n    32→from uuid import UUID, uuid4\n    33→\n    34→import httpx\n    35→import structlog\n    36→import yaml\n    37→\n    38→from backend.agents.discovery.schemas import SearchManifestSchema, DiscoveredJobSchema\n    39→\n    40→logger = structlog.get_logger(__name__)\n    41→\n    42→USER_AGENT = \"TalentAgent/1.0 (+https://github.com/example/talent-agent)\"\n    43→HTTP_TIMEOUT = 15.0\n    44→PER_SOURCE_CONCURRENCY = 4\n    45→SOURCES_YAML = Path(__file__).parent / \"sources.yaml\"\n    46→\n    47→\n    48→# ─── Offline fallback fixture data ────────────────────────────────────────────\n    49→# Used only when all live adapters return zero rows (network down or all\n    50→# sources unreachable). The `crawler.fallback_used` log event fires when this\n    51→# kicks in so prod can alert on it.\n    52→\n    53→_FALLBACK_JOBS: list[dict] = [\n    54→    {\n    55→        \"source\": \"greenhouse\",\n    56→        \"source_id\": \"gh-fixture-001\",\n    57→        \"title\": \"Head of AI Engineering\",\n    58→        \"company\": \"MusicTech AI\",\n    59→        \"location\": \"Remote (US)\",\n    60→        \"url\": \"https://boards.greenhouse.io/musictech/jobs/001\",\n    61→        \"description\": \"\"\"\n    62→We're a Series B music-tech startup building AI tools for creators and artists.\n    63→\n    64→Looking for a Head of AI Engineering to define our AI strategy from scratch.\n    65→You'll lead a team of ML engineers and shape the technical direction of our\n    66→AI-powered music recommendation and generation systems.\n    67→\n    68→Required:\n    69→- Python, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, Redis\n    70→- LLMs, Claude API, OpenAI API\n    71→- 8+ years engineering experience\n    72→- 3+ years in leadership roles\n    73→\n    74→Preferred:\n    75→- Kubernetes, Docker\n    76→- Music or audio domain experience\n    77→- Startup experience\n    78→\n    79→This is a 0-to-1 greenfield role. You'll shape the technical strategy,\n    80→build the team from scratch, and report directly to the CTO.\n    81→\n    82→Compensation: $250,000-$350,000 + 0.5-1.0% equity\n    83→\n    84→Remote-first. Mission-driven team.\n    85→Industry: Music, AI, Creator Economy\n    86→        \"\"\",\n    87→        \"salary_min\": 250000,\n    88→        \"salary_max\": 350000,\n    89→        \"remote\": True,\n    90→    },\n    91→    {\n    92→        \"source\": \"lever\",\n    93→        \"source_id\": \"lever-fixture-002\",\n    94→        \"title\": \"VP of Engineering\",\n    95→        \"company\": \"FinTech Startup\",\n    96→        \"location\": \"Miami, FL / Remote\",\n    97→        \"url\": \"https://jobs.lever.co/fintechstartup/002\",\n    98→        \"description\": \"\"\"\n    99→Fast-growing fintech startup looking for a VP of Engineering to scale our\n   100→platform from Series A to B.\n   101→\n   102→You'll own the entire engineering organization (currently 15 engineers) and\n   103→drive our technical roadmap as we expand into new markets.\n   104→\n   105→Requirements:\n   106→- 10+ years software engineering\n   107→- 5+ years in engineering leadership\n   108→- Java, Spring Boot, microservices\n   109→- AWS, Kubernetes, distributed systems\n   110→- Fintech or regulated industry experience\n   111→\n   112→What you'll do:\n   113→- Build and scale the engineering team to 40+ engineers\n   114→- Define technical strategy and architecture\n   115→- Partner with Product and Design leadership\n   116→- Establish engineering culture and processes\n   117→\n   118→Compensation: $300,000-$400,000 base + equity\n   119→Location: Miami preferred, remote considered\n   120→Industry: Fintech, Payments\n   121→        \"\"\",\n   122→        \"salary_min\": 300000,\n   123→        \"salary_max\": 400000,\n   124→        \"remote\": True,\n   125→    },\n   126→    {\n   127→        \"source\": \"ashby\",\n   128→        \"source_id\": \"ashby-fixture-003\",\n   129→        \"title\": \"Principal AI Engineer\",\n   130→        \"company\": \"AI Creative Studio\",\n   131→        \"location\": \"San Francisco, CA / Remote\",\n   132→        \"url\": \"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/aicreative/003\",\n   133→        \"description\": \"\"\"\n   134→We're building the future of AI-powered creative tools. Our platform helps\n   135→artists, musicians, and creators bring their visions to life.\n   136→\n   1